      "hints": [
        "Rearrange $(x-3)^2 = \\frac{x+11}{2}$.",
        "Take negative root: $g^{-1}(x) = 3 - \\sqrt{\\frac{x+11}{2}}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Set $y = 2(x - 3)^2 - 11$ and make $(x - 3)^2$ the subject:\n$$2(x - 3)^2 = y + 11 \\implies (x - 3)^2 = \\frac{y + 11}{2}$$",
        "Take the negative square root since $x \\le 3$:\n$$x - 3 = -\\sqrt{\\frac{y + 11}{2}} \\implies x = 3 - \\sqrt{\\frac{y + 11}{2}}$$",
